<%# Slice 7b (Gate 4): the gated profile header for a PRIVATE account the viewer may
    not see. Whitelisted fields only — avatar, full name, @handle, a "private account"
    notice, the follow/request button, and the follower/following COUNTS. Deliberately
    NO hoojah list, headline, location, link, or badges (those would leak content).
    Root carries dom_id(user, :profile_header) so a follow Turbo Stream can replace it.
    Locals: user.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.4) — ProfileHeader.prompt.md's `gated` variant is
    this exact whitelist: "avatar, name, handle, lock note, follow control and
    follower/following counts only; no headline, location, link, badges or hoojah list."
    So the ONLY change here is the avatar moving onto `ui/_avatar` (same 96px `lg` box,
    but survives a blank photo instead of raising). Do not "complete" this header by
    borrowing a row from `_profile_header` — every field absent below is absent on
    purpose, and spec/system/private_spec.rb is what notices. %>
<div id="<%= dom_id(user, :profile_header) %>"
     class="w-full bg-primary text-white fill-white flex flex-col items-center py-6 px-4">
  <%= render "ui/avatar", user: user, size: :lg, class: "mb-3" %>
  <h5 class="mb-0 text-lg font-medium"><%= user.full_name %></h5>
  <div class="mb-3">@<%= user.username %></div>

  <div class="mb-3 flex items-center gap-1 text-sm">
    <%= lucide_icon("lock", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
    <span>This account is private</span>
  </div>

  <%# Follow / request button (signed-in non-owner only; self-wraps in dom_id). %>
  <div class="mb-3">
    <%= render "follow_button", user: user %>
  </div>

  <%# Counts only — accepted-follower counts, no list link content leaks. %>
  <div class="text-sm mt-1 flex items-center gap-1">
    <%= link_to user_followers_path(user.username), class: "flex items-center gap-1 text-white" do %>
      <%= render "follower_count", user: user %>
    <% end %>
    <span class="mx-2">·</span>
    <%= link_to user_following_path(user.username), class: "flex items-center gap-1 text-white" do %>
      <%= lucide_icon("user-plus", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <span><%= user.following.size %></span>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
